abstract: >-
  Maple worksheets and procedures, with the computed spectra, for the quasinormal modes of scalar, electromagnetic and
  gravitational perturbations of black holes improved by a running Newton coupling: Planck stars, Bonanno–Reuter black
  holes and Hayward black holes, from the Schwarzschild limit to extremality. A Chebyshev collocation of the
  compactified radial equation in multiprecision arithmetic gives a quadratic eigenvalue problem, whose converged
  eigenvalues are listed in 186 reports. For the Hayward black holes the whole chain is included: the Maple assembly of
  the matrices, the MATLAB script that solves the eigenvalue problem with the Advanpix toolbox and writes the reports,
  and the Python driver that runs both for every set of parameters.
